mulations I showed is that they  just have so much data that GPU Ram is  the limiting factor  yes the question who is the consumers  for all this  yeah the Gates Foundation is the biggest  one and the one who fund most of it but  that's starting to change where we're  working a lot with countries themselves  we're working with NGOs that focus on  particular diseases or countries and  we're seeing a lot of uptake just  basically anyone who holds the purse  strings for health money is kind of  interested in this work so the size is  we typically have about 500 different  diseases and 30 20 age groups we do it  over 70 years for 50 risk factors and we  look at about five different ways of  measuring the outcomes and then we do  about 50,000 draws from the uncertainty  estimation so it comes out to a little  over a petabyte of storage for that we  try to work on some short-term things  it's a little bit harder because we as  an organization we require grants to  fund these things and it's hard to get a  quick turnaround those but we actually  just got a grant for some Ebola work  right now
 

